From 44c2793d5334a72d995db39c43e24518d53cb3bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:38:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Report the real error when a container facts lookup fails

The failure handler in kolla_container_facts is

    module.fail_json(changed=True, msg=repr(format_exc()),
                     **getattr(cfw, 'result', {}))

and ContainerFactsWorker.__init__ seeds self.result with
dict(changed=False). So changed arrives twice, once as the explicit
keyword and once from the ** expansion, and fail_json raises

    TypeError: AnsibleModule.fail_json() got multiple values for
    keyword argument 'changed'

before it writes any JSON. The module produces no stdout at all and
Ansible reports "MODULE FAILURE: No start of json char found", while the
exception the handler was built to report survives only inside
module_stderr, several frames down.

Drop the explicit changed=True. The worker's own result dict already
carries changed, so the expansion supplies it, and the real traceback
reaches the operator.

This became reachable in commit 19af5826f, which renamed
ContainerFactsWorker.results to result. Before that the getattr lookup
for 'result' found nothing, returned an empty dict, and nothing
collided.

Signed-off-by: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
---
 ansible/library/kolla_container_facts.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ansible/library/kolla_container_facts.py b/ansible/library/kolla_container_facts.py
index 47d5351c0..509a18ec3 100644
--- a/ansible/library/kolla_container_facts.py
+++ b/ansible/library/kolla_container_facts.py
@@ -256,7 +256,7 @@ def main():
         result = bool(getattr(cfw, module.params.get('action'))())
         module.exit_json(result=result, **cfw.result)
     except Exception:
-        module.fail_json(changed=True, msg=repr(format_exc()),
+        module.fail_json(msg=repr(format_exc()),
                          **getattr(cfw, 'result', {}))
 
 
